at `catalog.text`, where the function actually lives.\n- **`catalog/books.py`**: `parse_book` stored the year as text (`'1965'`), so `age()` crashed when subtracting it. It now converts the year to an integer.\n- **`catalog/factory.py`**: `sample_books()` was missing `Emma`, though its own docstring lists three titles. I added `Book(\"Emma\", \"Austen\", 1815, 1)`. The author, year and copy count are my choice; the tests only check the title.\n- **`catalog/fees.py`**: the fee was days late *plus* the daily rate instead of *times* it, so one day cost 1.25 instead of 0.25. It's now `days_late * DAILY_FEE`.\n- **`catalog/inventory.py`**: `recent(n)` returned one event too many. It now returns the last `n`, and an empty list when `n` is 0 or less, since slicing with `[-0:]` would otherwise return the whole history.\n- **`catalog/members.py`**: `MAX_BORROWED` was 3, but the comment above it and the tests both say members can hold five books. I set it to 5.", "paced_wait_s": null, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "run_id": "opencode:make-ci-green:claude-opus-5-5:trial2", "sampling_observed": null, "score": 1.0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 24.55, "t_checker_s": 0.178, "t_env_setup_s": 0.002, "task": "make-ci-green", "timeout_s": 2400, "token_basis": "vendor_split", "token_basis_proxy": null, "tokens": 1480, "tokens_cache_read": 82512, "tokens_cache_write": 40386, "tokens_fresh": 1480, "tokens_input_uncached": 14, "tokens_output": 1466, "tokens_proxy_cache_read": null, "tokens_proxy_cache_write": null, "tokens_proxy_calls": null, "tokens_proxy_input_uncached": null, "tokens_proxy_output": null, "tokens_proxy_reasoning": null, "tokens_reasoning": 0, "trial": 2, "ts_iso": "2026-10-04T23:36:40", "turns": 6, "usage_raw": [{"cache": {"read": 0, "write": 15666}, "input": 4, "output": 101, "reasoning": 0, "total": 15771}, {"cache": {"read": 15666, "write": 2039}, "input": 2, "output": 125, "reasoning": 0, "total": 17832}, {"cache": {"read": 0, "write": 21948}, "inp